    "diagnosis": "petco (PET multiplier) is pinned at its allowed maximum of 1.20 in the calibrated set. Independently, TerraClimate indicates SWAT+ ET is ~12.5% too low. Two separate lines of evidence therefore agree that the model wants more evapotranspiration than the parameter range permits."
  },
  "honest_status": {
    "et_independent_check": "PARTIAL - against MODIS MOD16 sampled over the true basin, volume is within 14.4% (inside the +/-25% Moriasi band) but seasonal dynamics are weak (monthly NSE 0.14). SWAT+ swings ~26 mm across the year against MODIS's ~86 mm, so the seasonal amplitude is roughly 3x too flat. TerraClimate independently shows the same pattern.",
    "hazard_map_pixel_level": "MODEST SKILL - AUC-ROC 0.62 against the 2012 MODIS flood extent; zone enrichment rises monotonically to 1.61x in Very High.",
    "hazard_map_lga_level": "INCONCLUSIVE - NEMA report counts track raw population (rho 0.57) far better than modelled exposure (rho 0.17), so the test is confounded by reporting effort and cannot validate the map.",
    "not_claimed": "None of this establishes forecast skill. The map remains an AHP susceptibility index, now with a measured and modest correspondence to one observed flood event."
  }
